node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Everything retrace generates lives under .retrace/ — run dirs, diff images,
# repro bundles — and none of it belongs in a commit. Ignore the directory's
# contents wholesale rather than naming each subdir as it is added, so a new
# generated location is covered the day it appears.
#
# The `.retrace/*` form matters: git cannot re-include a path whose PARENT
# directory is excluded, so a blanket `.retrace/` would make the negation
# below dead. Ignoring the entries instead leaves the directory itself
# traversable.
#
# The recording team key is a secret: it comes from RETRACE_RECORDING_KEY or
# .retrace/recording.key, and must never be committed. It is covered here.
.retrace/*
# ...except the machine-owned wire-rule overlay, which IS committed — it is
# the reviewed record of which fields are allowed to vary (config.OverlayPath).
!.retrace/wire-rules.json
#
# Reference bundles ARE committed — .retrace-ref/<app>/<flow>/reference is
# the blessed artifact a diff runs against, and an ignored bundle is a diff
# that silently has nothing to compare against on a fresh clone. There is
# deliberately NO pattern for it here: it lives OUTSIDE .retrace/ precisely
# so the blanket rule above cannot swallow it. Do not "tidy" the two roots
# into one. The repro bundles `retrace ref reject` emits are the opposite —
# throwaway attachments for a bug report — and land under .retrace/repro/,
# which line 17 already covers; naming it explicitly would contradict the
# wholesale rule stated above, so it is not named.
coverage/
bin/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, reports, review
# packages. Local coordination state, never part of the source tree.
.superpowers/

# Dashboard build output is embedded via go:embed (ensemble/server/ui/ui.go).
# Only the placeholder ensemble/server/ui/dist/index.html is committed — the
# blanket `dist/` rule above would otherwise swallow it too, so unignore
# this dist/ specifically and its index.html, then re-ignore the built
# assets/ subtree. `pnpm -r build` overwrites index.html locally with the
# real bundle, which must never land in a commit — `git restore
# ensemble/server/ui/dist/index.html` after building, before committing.
!ensemble/server/ui/dist/
!ensemble/server/ui/dist/index.html
ensemble/server/ui/dist/assets/
